s://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0016", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.3287, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0003", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2349, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0028", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.1603, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__mdna__0008", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7654, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__unknown__0015", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "unknown", "score": 0.6539, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__unknown__0008", "ticker": "AAPL", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-09-27", "section": "unknown", "score": 0.6279, "filing_name": "Apple Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019325000079/aapl-20250927.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 4, "dropped_candidates": 52, "token_estimate": 31963, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Apple's fiscal 2025 10-K (ended September 27, 2025) groups its risk factors under macroeconomic and industry risks, business risks, legal and regulatory compliance risks, financial risks, and general risks. Macroeconomic risks include adverse global economic conditions and international trade restrictions such as the U.S. Tariffs announced beginning in the second quarter of 2025 [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000] [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0003]. Business risks include reliance on outsourcing partners and single-source components, and intense competition [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008] [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0005]. Legal and regulatory risks include antitrust suits, EU Digital Markets Act compliance, and the Google search-licensing remedies [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0026] [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0027]. Financial risks include gross margin pressure, foreign exchange exposure, and tax changes [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0030] [AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0031]. The filing does not rank these risks, and the Q1 fiscal 2026 10-Q (ended December 27, 2025) reports no material changes to them [AAPL_10Q_2025-12-27__legal_proceedings__0003].", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "company": "Apple Inc", "findings": [{"point": "Macroeconomic and trade risks: adverse global economic conditions can reduce demand, and restrictions on international trade (tariffs, import/export controls) can harm its business and supply chain, including the U.S. Tariffs announced beginning in the second quarter of 2025.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0003"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Business and supply chain risks: a significant majority of manufacturing is done by outsourcing partners in Asia, many components come from single or limited sources, and markets are highly competitive.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0005"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Legal and regulatory risks: Apple faces antitrust investigations and litigation, DMA compliance obligations in the EU, and potential remedies affecting its Google search licensing revenue.", "citations": ["AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0026", "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0027"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": null, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0000", "claim": "Adverse economic conditions can reduce demand for Apple's products and services.", "quote": "Adverse macroeconomic conditions, including slow growth or recession, high unemployment, inflation, tighter credit, higher interest rates, and currency fluctuations"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0003", "claim": "New U.S. Tariffs were announced beginning in the second quarter of 2025.", "quote": "Beginning in the second quarter of 2025, new tariffs were announced on imports to the U.S."}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0008", "claim": "Manufacturing relies on outsourcing partners and single-source suppliers.", "quote": "The Company relies on single-source partners in the U.S., Asia and Europe to supply and manufacture many components"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0005", "claim": "Apple's markets are highly competitive and subject to rapid technological change.", "quote": "Global markets for the Company's products and services are highly competitive and subject to rapid technological change"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0026", "claim": "Apple faces DMA compliance obligations and antitrust litigation.", "quote": "The DMA provides for significant fines and penalties for noncompliance."}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0027", "claim": "Google-related remedies could affect Apple's search licensing revenue.", "quote": "A reversal of the order on appeal could result in imposition of certain remedies initially proposed by the DOJ"}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0030", "claim": "Net sales and gross margins face volatility and downward pressure.", "quote": "The Company's net sales and gross margins are subject to volatility and downward pressure due to a variety of factors."}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10K_2025-09-27__risk_factors__0031", "claim": "Apple's financial performance is subject to foreign exchange risk.", "quote": "The Company's financial performance is subject to risks associated with changes in the value of the U.S. dollar relative to local currencies."}, {"chunk_id": "AAPL_10Q_2025-12-27__legal_proceedings__0003", "claim": "The Q1 fiscal 2026 10-Q reports no material changes to the risk factors.", "quote": "There have been no material changes to the Company's risk factors since the 2025 Form 10-K."}], "coverage": {"companies_used": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "forms": ["10-K", "10-Q"], "fiscal_periods": ["FY2025, ended September 27, 2025", "Q1 FY2026, ended December 27, 2025"]}], "companies_missing": [], "data_as_of": "2026-01-30"}, "gaps": ["The filing does not rank its risks by severity or likelihood, so no ranking is given.", "The risk factors section is only partly summarized; other themes (cybersecurity, talent, reseller dependence, credit, stock price volatility) are present in the filing but not detailed here."], "confidence": "high", "confidence_reason": "The 10-K risk factor chunks cover the full section and the 10-Q confirms no material changes, though the answer summarizes rather than exhaustively lists every risk.", "next_questions": ["How does Apple describe its tariff and supply chain exposure in the fiscal 2025 10-K?", "What does Apple say about 